# Apex 26 — Cursor entry

- **Rules:** read root `AGENTS.md` (canonical). Root `CLAUDE.md` is a stub that
  imports it; do not edit rules into `CLAUDE.md`.
- **Skills / subagents:** `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` and `.claude/agents/*.md`
  (shared with Claude Code). Codex reads the same skill bodies via
  `.agents/skills/<name>` (`bash tools/env/mirror-skills.sh` fills it) — keep
  lockstep, never fork. Do not add `.cursor/skills/` or `.cursor/agents/`
  unless a file is explicitly Cursor-only. The glob rules here (`render-wgx`,
  `render-tlx`) carry the same bodies as `.claude/rules/` — edit both.
- **Route:** deploy/`version.json` → `deploy-research` (host fetch / WebFetch);
  pre-push → `verify-agent` (`--base <ref>` for "was it already red?");
  live canvas → `mcp-probe`; host browser → `playwright-official`;
  bloat/extract/dead code → `slim-bloat` / `bloat-auditor`. Do not attach
  `mcp-probe` for a version.json check.
- **MCP:** three servers in root `.mcp.json` (and `.cursor/mcp.json`):
  `apex-tools`, `playwright-official`, `chrome-devtools`. Cloud host catalog
  often does **not** auto-load them — then `tools/mcp/apex-tools-mcp.sh call`,
  `tools/mcp/chrome-devtools-mcp.sh`, `python3 tools/mcp/probe-mcp.py chrome-start`
  (CLI daemon, not attached). `tools/mcp/tinyfish-mcp.sh` is CLI-only and
  egress-blocked in-container. Map: `docs/AGENT-SURFACE.md`. The browser rules
  (one at a time, never inside a subagent) are AGENTS.md §Verification.
- **Cursor Cloud (moved from AGENTS.md):** launch with model id `default` only. Cloud MCP is always
  `cursor` / `cursor-cloud` / `cursor-subscriptions`, plus `apex-tools` / `chrome-devtools` /
  `playwright-official` after Bootstrap §3; if only the three `cursor*` appear, use the CLI fallbacks
  above, invent no namespace, and re-Save when `environment-info` shows nameless bare-`bash` allowlist
  rows. After every PR push: `subscribe_github_ci` + `subscribe_github_pr`; one timer
  check-in (~1 h) only if the host lists `subscribe_timer` / `send_later` (do not invent it). Serve
  locally for browser checks (the VM rarely reaches github.io). using-superpowers / brainstorming
  hard-gates are optional references; AGENTS.md and the skills win.
- **Token hygiene:** one skill per task; prefer `__apex` / `verify-track` /
  `test:tooling-fast` before screenshots or browser groups. Path-scoped rules
  under `.cursor/rules/` (e.g. `render-wgx.mdc`, `render-tlx.mdc`) attach by
  globs. Bootstrap / Cloud MCP: `docs/AGENT-SURFACE.md` §Bootstrap.
